Adriano,
Many thanks for this very thorough implementation and investigation.

I'm not an expert in this domain, so I hope we'll get feedback from others, but as far as I'm concerned updating and correcting test cases is part of normal development, so if we agree that reproducing the output of GNU R is the criteria by which we judge renjin's implementation, than it's logical that you update the test cases to match the output of GNU R.

I'd still be curious to have tests against other measures of correctness, maybe something like this: http://csrc.nist.gov/groups/ST/toolkit/rng/documents/SP800-22rev1a.pdf  ? But reproducing GNU-R's output bit-by-bit would be a great first step!

All the best,

Alex

